  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through a chain of indications involving Tretamine. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may be used to treat various ovarian tumors, including Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, Familial Ovarian Cancer, and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary, all of which are indicated to respond to Tretamine. This implies a potential pathway where Thiotepa could influence the progression or treatment of ovarian small cell carcinoma, possibly through mechanisms involving Tretamine. The shared indication of Tretamine with ovarian small cell carcinoma suggests a possible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role for Thiotepa in the treatment of ovarian small cell carcinoma, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanisms and clinical relevance.",
